<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">Captaincy General of Chile</h1><p class="st-meta">1541 CE – 1818 CE · capital Santiago</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Spain's southernmost colony in the Americas, a frontier realm defined by a long war against the Mapuche and later the birthplace of the Chilean republic.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pedro-de-valdivia">Pedro de Valdivia</a> led an expedition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-jamaica">Santiago</a> in February 1541. He extended Spanish settlement south, founding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/concepcion-chile">Concepción</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valdivia">Valdivia</a>, but was killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">the Mapuche</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lautaro">Lautaro</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-tucapel">Tucapel</a> in 1553. The territory was governed as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a> within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/viceroyalty-of-peru">Viceroyalty of Peru</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Chile's governor was also captain-general because of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arauco-war">Arauco War</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mapuche">the Mapuche</a>. After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/araucania">Mapuche</a> victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-curalaba">Curalaba</a> in 1598 destroyed the southern towns, the frontier settled on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biobio-river">Biobío</a> river with a permanent army. The Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/audiencia">Audiencia</a> sat at <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/spanish-jamaica">Santiago</a> from 1609. The economy rested on wheat, tallow and livestock sold to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, worked on large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hacienda">haciendas</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bourbon-reforms">Bourbon reforms</a> made <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a> a captaincy general more independent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in 1798.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> junta took power in 1810, opening the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/patria-vieja">Patria Vieja</a>. Royalist forces regained control in 1814, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-ohiggins">Bernardo O'Higgins</a> won at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chacabuco">Chacabuco</a> in 1817 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-maipu">Maipú</a> in 1818, when <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a> declared independence as the Republic of Chile.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/captaincy-general-of-chile.jpg" alt="Captaincy General of Chile" width="320" height="321"><figcaption>Image: B1mbo · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Captaincy_General_of_Chile_(orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1541 CE – 1818 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Santiago</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Pedro de Valdivia, Ambrosio O'Higgins</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/chile">Chile</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Chile, Governorate of Chile, Reino de Chile</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1680&amp;focus=captaincy-general-of-chile" aria-label="Captaincy General of Chile on the atlas"><svg c